cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use HamLeT in your work, please cite this software and the model-specific references in the relevant model card."
title: "HamLeT: Hamiltonian Learning Toolkit"
type: software
abstract: "An experimental-facing framework for learning Hamiltonians and physical parameters from STM/STS data, with spin chains as its first implemented physics mode."
authors:
  - family-names: Lupi
    given-names: Greta
version: 0.1.0
license: GPL-3.0-or-later
repository-code: "https://github.com/GretaLupi/hamlet-toolkit"
url: "https://github.com/GretaLupi/hamlet-toolkit"
keywords:
  - Hamiltonian learning
  - spin chains
  - scanning tunneling spectroscopy
  - machine learning
# The physics this package implements. The models trained for these papers are
# not distributed here; the package provides the same Hamiltonian families and
# measurement logic so an equivalent model can be trained.
references:
